iles were associated with oral cancer-free survival and used to develope multivariate predictive models for oral cancer prediction. We developed a 29-transcript predictive model which showed marked improvement in terms of prediction accuracy (with 8% predicting error rate) over the models using previously known clinico-pathological risk factors. Based on the gene expression profile data, we also identified 2182 transcripts significantly associated with oral cancer risk associated genes (P-value<0.01, single variate Cox proportional hazards model). Functional pathway analysis revealed proteasome machinery, MYC, and ribosomes components as the top gene sets associated with oral cancer risk. In multiple independent datasets, the expression profiles of the genes can differentiate head and neck cancer from normal mucosa.  Our results show that gene expression profiles may improve the prediction of oral cancer risk in OPL patients and the significant genes identified may serve as potential targets for oral cancer chemoprevention.","gpl":"6244","gse":"26549","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by array","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2011/02/01","suppfile":"CEL","samples":[{"accession":"GSM652792","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM363"},{"accession":"GSM652838","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM409"},{"accession":"GSM652798","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM369"},{"accession":"GSM652835","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM406"},{"accession":"GSM652772","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM341"},{"accession":"GSM652818","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM389"},{"accession":"GSM652775","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM344"},{"accession":"GSM652815","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM386"},{"accession":"GSM652795","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM366"},{"accession":"GSM652812","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM383"},{"accession":"GSM652801","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM372"},{"accession":"GSM652764","title":"Oral leukoplakia LM333"},{"accession":"GSM652761","title":"Ora