 (HNSCC) sampleNo.11"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":23,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["18661521","29423074"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE9nnn/GSE9638/","geo2r":"yes","bioproject":"PRJNA103497"},"200006791":{"uid":"200006791","accession":"GSE6791","gds":"","title":"Gene Expression Profiles of HPV-Positive and -Negative Head/Neck and Cervical Cancers","summary":"Human papillomaviruses (HPVs) are associated with nearly all cervical cancers (CCs), 20-30% of head and neck cancers (HNCs), and other cancers. Because HNCs also arise in HPV-negative patients, this type of cancer provides unique opportunities to define similarities and differences of HPV-positive versus HPV-negative cancers arising in the same tissue.  Here, we describe genome-wide expression profiling of 84 HNCs, CCs and site-matched normal epithelial samples in which we used laser capture microdissection to enrich samples for tumor-derived versus normal epithelial cells.  This analysis revealed that HPV+HNCs and CCs differed in their patterns of gene expression yet shared many changes compared to HPV-HNCs. Some of these shared changes were predicted, but many others were not. Notably, HPV+HNCs and CCs were found to be upregulated in their expression of a distinct and larger subset of cell cycle genes than observed in HPV-HNC.  Moreover, HPV+ cancers over-expressed testis-specific genes that are normally expressed only in meiotic cells.  Many, though not all, of the hallmark differences between HPV+HNC and HPV-HNC were a direct consequence of HPV and in particular the viral E6 and E7 oncogenes. This included a novel association of HPV oncogenes with testes specific gene expression. These findings in primary human tumors provide novel biomarkers for early detection of HPV+ and HPV- cancers, and emphasize the potential value of targeting E6 and E7 function, alone or combined with radiation and/or traditional chemotherapy, in the treatment of HPV+ cancers. Keywords: Gene expression ptofiles of primary cancers","gpl":"570","gse":"6791","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by array","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2007/05/15","suppfile":"CEL, EXP","samples":[{"accession":"GSM155684","title":"HNC2714"},{"accession":"GSM155647","title":"CC029"},{"accession":"GSM155664","title":"CC701"},{"accession":"GSM155704","title":"HNC2966"},{"accession":"GSM155710","title":"HNC3687"},{"accession":"GSM155667","title":"CN022"},{"accession":"GSM155661","title":"CC519"},{"accession":"GSM155707","title":"HNC3046"},{"accession":"GSM155687","title":"HNC2725"},{"accession":"GSM155724","title":"ND012"},{"accession":"GSM155727","title":"ND017"},{"accession":"GSM155693","title":"HNC2814"},{"accession":"GSM155673","title":"HNC004"},{"accession":"GSM155676","title":"HNC008"},{"accession":"GSM155670","title":"CN407"},{"accession":"GSM155713","title":"HNCS2"},{"accession":"GSM155696","title":"HNC2855"},{"accession":"GSM155650","title":"CC068"},{"accession":"GSM155716","title":"HNN023"},{"accession":"GSM155653","title":"CC233"},{"accession":"GSM155690","title":"HNC2748"},{"accession":"GSM155702","title":"HNC2914"},{"accession":"GSM155656","title":"CC300"},{"accession":"GSM155719","title":"HNN053"},{"accession":"GSM155705","title":"HNC2967"},{"accession":"GSM155722","title":"ND010"},{"accession":"GSM155679","title":"HNC015"},{"accession":"GSM155725","title":"ND014"},{"accession":"GSM155659","title":"CC507"},{"accession":"GSM155682","title":"HNC2551"},{"accession":"GSM155699","title":"HNC2887"},{"accession":"GSM155711","title":"HNCB1"},{"accession":"GSM155648","title":"CC034A"},{"accession":"GSM155685","title":"HNC2719"},{"accession":"GSM155688","title":"HNC2738"},{"accession":"GSM155662","title":"CC553"},{"accession":"GSM155645","title":"CC010"},{"accession":"GSM155728","title":"ND018"},{"accession":"GSM155665","title":"CN001"},{"a